# Git & polyrepo conventions

- Polyrepo: `rba-features`, `rba-contracts`, `rba-decision-service`, `rba-idp`,
 `rba-ml-training`, `rba-infra`, `docs` are independent repos on `github.com/roku-pfi`,
 cloned side-by-side. `rba-ml-training` installs `rba-features` editable via
 `../rba-features`; decision-service pins both `rba-features` and `rba-contracts`;
 `rba-idp` pins `rba-contracts`. Shared Redis/Postgres compose lives in `rba-infra`
 (not in service repos).
- Commit messages: Conventional Commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, `docs:`, with an
  optional scope like `feat(ml):`). Pass the body via a HEREDOC.
- Only commit when asked. Push to `main` is a protected action — surface it for
  approval, never force-push.
- NEVER modify git config. NEVER commit data or secrets: datasets (`data/raw/`,
  `data/subset/`, `*.csv`, `*.parquet`), venvs, artifacts/reports, and `.cursor/mcp.json`
  contents stay out of version control.
- Keep changes scoped to one repo per commit; a change spanning repos = one commit each.
